{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1559544185,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NTEzMTY4OTU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3469","origin":"github"},"title":"`install()` misinterprets relative path","message":"We decided that in the cmdline, relative is always relative to PWD. This is not what happens in `install`\n\n```\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad install -d bids -s raw bids/sourcedata\n[INFO   ] Cloning raw into '/tmp/bids/bids/bids/sourcedata' \ninstall(ok): bids/bids/sourcedata (dataset)                                                  \naction summary:\n  add (ok: 2)\n  install (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n(datalad3-dev) mih@meiner /tmp % datalad subdatasets -d bids\nsubdataset(ok): bids/bids/sourcedata (dataset)\n```\n\nSo while the relative path given as source (`-s`) is treated as being relative to PWD, the target path is treated as being relative to the specified dataset path.","files":null}]}